<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imagawa Yoshimoto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1519">1519</a>–<a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imagawa Yoshimoto was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> who ruled Suruga, Tōtōmi and Mikawa from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunpu">Sunpu</a>, one of the most powerful lords of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Marching towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> in 1560, he was killed in a surprise attack by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>'s much smaller force at Okehazama. His death led to the decline of the Imagawa and the rise of Nobunaga.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imagawa-yoshimoto.jpg" alt="Imagawa Yoshimoto" width="320" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ImagawaYoshimoto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
